# 7. Evidence provenance is currently wired incorrectly

This one is structurally serious.

Your SQL model says:

```text
evidence.observation_id
        ↓ FK
source_observations.observation_id
```

That is correct.

But investigation currently creates evidence with:

```ts
observationId:
  notes.searchId ?? "synthetic"
```

A **SerpApi search ID is not an official-source observation ID**.

Those are two separate provenance chains:

```text
DISCOVERY

SerpApi SearchRun
    ↓
SearchResult
    ↓
Candidate


VERIFICATION

Candidate
    ↓
Source
    ↓
SourceObservation
    ↓
Evidence
    ↓
Fact
```

Do not collapse them.

Your database already has the right conceptual separation. The implementation needs to follow it.

And because foreign keys are enabled in `openDb()`, this wiring should also be tested against a completely fresh database.

