# 24. “37 passing tests” is good, but the next 37 matter more

The current tests are legitimately useful—they cover the request canonicalizer, normalization, prefiltering, scheduler, hashes, URLs and replay radar.

But now the danger sits downstream.

## Anti-cheat test suite I would add

| Test                              | Expected failure if system is cheating/wrong        |
| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| **Replay/live parity**            | Replay produces a fact live validation would reject |
| **Missing source fixture**        | Any synthetic fallback is generated                 |
| **Missing AI fixture**            | System silently fabricates extraction               |
| **No-network replay**             | Any `fetch()` occurs in replay mode                 |
| **Bad evidence quote**            | Fact accepted when quote isn't present              |
| **Unsupported number**            | Quote says no number but AI invents one             |
| **$0.01/1K conversion**           | Anything except $10/1M                              |
| **$25/100M conversion**           | Anything except $0.25/1M                            |
| **Unknown field**                 | `made_up_price` accepted                            |
| **Wrong unit/field**              | requests/day stored as tokens/day                   |
| **Official-domain spoof**         | `openai.com.evil.test` accepted                     |
| **Query-string spoof**            | `evil.test/?q=openai.com` accepted                  |
| **SSRF**                          | localhost/private/link-local fetched                |
| **Official → private redirect**   | redirect followed                                   |
| **News-vs-source conflict**       | SERP snippet overwrites official fact               |
| **Search result shuffle**         | candidate's evidence source changes incorrectly     |
| **Duplicate story**               | multiple stories create multiple same events        |
| **Same fact again**               | new fact row/change event generated                 |
| **First fact**                    | counted as a changed previous fact                  |
| **Supersession failure**          | old fact closed without replacement                 |
| **Synthetic fixture isolation**   | synthetic data visible in production mode           |
| **Build freshness**               | rebuild changes verified/observed timestamp         |
| **Page freshness**                | browser render time shown as verification time      |
| **Quota reserve**                 | live radar can spend below reserve                  |
| **Concurrent identical query**    | more than one SerpApi call                          |
| **force_fresh override**          | caller can disable `no_cache`                       |
| **Randomized provider names**     | same hard-coded facts magically emerge              |
| **Delete fixture**                | demo continues successfully                         |
| **Clean DB E2E**                  | provenance foreign keys fail                        |
| **All verified facts provenance** | any verified fact lacks source observation          |
| **Snippet-as-evidence audit**     | search result is authoritative evidence             |

The most important CI invariant should literally be:

```text
every verified fact
→ evidence
→ source observation
→ authoritative source
```

and separately:

```text
candidate
→ search result
→ SerpApi search run
```

Those chains may meet through the candidate, but must not be confused.

