# 40. Cloudflare's `$3.30/month equivalent` is arithmetic, not cash value

LLMDeals says:

> “$3.30/mo equivalent value at paid rates.”

Calculation:

```text
10,000 neurons/day
× 30 days
= 300,000

300 × $0.011/1K
= $3.30
```

So the arithmetic is correct. Current Cloudflare pricing confirms both numbers. ([Cloudflare Docs][2])

But call it:

> **reference value at paid marginal rate**

not generic economic “value.”

Free-plan users can't necessarily simply consume that as cash-equivalent paid usage, and current model eligibility has paid-billing caveats. ([Cloudflare Docs][2])

